<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for cel-cortex-daemon.

  The daemon binary is bundled inside Cellar.app at
  Contents/Resources/cel-cortex-daemon, then copied at first launch
  to ~/.cellar/bin/cel-cortex-daemon and managed by the LaunchAgent
  at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cellar.daemon.plist (Docker-style
  lifecycle — see cellar-app-v1.md §14).

  The daemon must be signed with hardened runtime + these entitlements
  BEFORE it is bundled into Cellar.app. The app-level signature does
  not transitively cover nested binaries; each binary needs its own
  signature against the same Developer ID.

  Differences from app/src-tauri/entitlements.plist:
    - No `allow-jit` (no WKWebView, no JS runtime).
    - No `allow-unsigned-executable-memory` (Rust-only, AOT-compiled).
    - Apple Events still required: the daemon hosts the embedded
      agent + cel_act gateway, which dispatches actions through the
      AppleScript-backed adapters (calendar, mail, messages, notes,
      reminders).
    - Library validation must stay disabled because the daemon loads
      adapter ProcessDriver binaries built by the same workspace.

  Accessibility (used by cel-accessibility for AX tree reads in the
  cortex tick loop) is a TCC grant, not an entitlement. The user
  grants it once from System Settings → Privacy & Security →
  Accessibility. Re-signing with a different identity invalidates
  the grant.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <false/>

    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
